[2026-03-15T00:11:59.685Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CpwXuL5JNYmpVrR7uqp3T5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary: Logout Handling in AirbnbClone\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase, here's how the app handles logout:\n\n### 1. Logout Button with data-testid\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` (lines 62-70)\n\n```typescript\n<button\n  data-testid=\"sidebar-logout\"\n  className=\"sidebar__link sidebar__logout\"\n  onClick={() => dispatch(logout())}\n  title={collapsed ? 'Log Out' : undefined}\n>\n  <LogoutIcon />\n  {!collapsed && <span>Log Out</span>}\n</button>\n```\n\nThe logout button has the testid `sidebar-logout` and dispatches the Redux `logout` action when clicked.\n\n### 2. Logout Route/API Endpoint\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts` (lines 113-117)\n\nThere is **no logout API endpoint**. Instead, logout is a local Redux reducer action:\n\n```typescript\nconst authSlice = createSlice({\n  name: 'auth',\n  initialState,\n  reducers: {\n    logout(state) {\n      state.currentUser = null\n      state.error = null\n      saveUserToStorage(null)\n    },\n    // ...\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe logout action:\n- Clears `currentUser` state\n- Clears any error messages\n- Removes the user from localStorage by calling `saveUserToStorage(null)` (line 116)\n\n### 3. How Test Files Handle Switching Between Users\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/my-trips-cards.spec.ts` (lines 3-14)\n\nThe pattern used across multiple test files (`my-trips-cards.spec.ts`, `favorite-button.spec.ts`, `host-dashboard-bookings.spec.ts`, etc.):\n\n```typescript\nasync function loginAs(page: import('@playwright/test').Page, email: string) {\n  // Log out first if already logged in\n  const logoutBtn = page.getByTestId('sidebar-logout')\n  if (await logoutBtn.isVisible().catch(() => false)) {\n    await logoutBtn.click()\n    await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/login/, { timeout: 30000 })\n  }\n  await page.goto('/login')\n  await page.getByTestId('login-email-input').fill(email)\n  await page.getByTestId('login-submit-button').click()\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/', { timeout: 30000 })\n}\n```\n\n**Usage pattern:** (from `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/my-trips-cards.spec.ts` lines 88-96)\n\n```typescript\n// Switch to Past tab for completed badge - blue\nawait page.getByTestId('tab-past').click()\nconst completedBadge = page.getByTestId('status-badge-e1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111')\nawait expect(completedBadge).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })\nawait expect(completedBadge).toHaveClass(/text-status-completed/)\n\n// Log in as Alex to check cancelled badge - red\nawait loginAs(page, 'alex@example.com')\nawait page.goto('/trips')\n```\n\nThe `loginAs` helper function automatically logs out the current user by clicking the `sidebar-logout` button before logging in as a different user."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: add6bc8903d6f45fc (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 36942\ntool_uses: 12\nduration_ms: 16125</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed4f3c62-e32b-47e8-ad73-d7f458349ef4","uuid":"5499e3c1-3f9a-496e-8897-09a2929cb87c","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In /repo/apps/AirbnbClone, find how the app handles logout. Look for:\n1. A logout button/link with a data-testid\n2. The logout route or API endpoint\n3. How other test files handle switching between users (loginAs then another loginAs)\nCheck files like tests/*.spec.ts for patterns of logging in as different users. Return relevant code snippets.","agentId":"add6bc8903d6f45fc","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the findings:\n\n## Summary: Logout Handling in AirbnbClone\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase, here's how the app handles logout:\n\n### 1. Logout Button with data-testid\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` (lines 62-70)\n\n```typescript\n<button\n  data-testid=\"sidebar-logout\"\n  className=\"sidebar__link sidebar__logout\"\n  onClick={() => dispatch(logout())}\n  title={collapsed ? 'Log Out' : undefined}\n>\n  <LogoutIcon />\n  {!collapsed && <span>Log Out</span>}\n</button>\n```\n\nThe logout button has the testid `sidebar-logout` and dispatches the Redux `logout` action when clicked.\n\n### 2. Logout Route/API Endpoint\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/src/slices/authSlice.ts` (lines 113-117)\n\nThere is **no logout API endpoint**. Instead, logout is a local Redux reducer action:\n\n```typescript\nconst authSlice = createSlice({\n  name: 'auth',\n  initialState,\n  reducers: {\n    logout(state) {\n      state.currentUser = null\n      state.error = null\n      saveUserToStorage(null)\n    },\n    // ...\n  },\n})\n```\n\nThe logout action:\n- Clears `currentUser` state\n- Clears any error messages\n- Removes the user from localStorage by calling `saveUserToStorage(null)` (line 116)\n\n### 3. How Test Files Handle Switching Between Users\n\n**File:** `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/my-trips-cards.spec.ts` (lines 3-14)\n\nThe pattern used across multiple test files (`my-trips-cards.spec.ts`, `favorite-button.spec.ts`, `host-dashboard-bookings.spec.ts`, etc.):\n\n```typescript\nasync function loginAs(page: import('@playwright/test').Page, email: string) {\n  // Log out first if already logged in\n  const logoutBtn = page.getByTestId('sidebar-logout')\n  if (await logoutBtn.isVisible().catch(() => false)) {\n    await logoutBtn.click()\n    await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\\/login/, { timeout: 30000 })\n  }\n  await page.goto('/login')\n  await page.getByTestId('login-email-input').fill(email)\n  await page.getByTestId('login-submit-button').click()\n  await expect(page).toHaveURL('/', { timeout: 30000 })\n}\n```\n\n**Usage pattern:** (from `/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/tests/my-trips-cards.spec.ts` lines 88-96)\n\n```typescript\n// Switch to Past tab for completed badge - blue\nawait page.getByTestId('tab-past').click()\nconst completedBadge = page.getByTestId('status-badge-e1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111')\nawait expect(completedBadge).toBeVisible({ timeout: 30000 })\nawait expect(completedBadge).toHaveClass(/text-status-completed/)\n\n// Log in as Alex to check cancelled badge - red\nawait loginAs(page, 'alex@example.com')\nawait page.goto('/trips')\n```\n\nThe `loginAs` helper function automatically logs out the current user by clicking the `sidebar-logout` button before logging in as a different user."}],"totalDurationMs":16125,"totalTokens":36942,"totalToolUseCount":12,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5275,"cache_read_input_tokens":30785,"output_tokens":877,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5275},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
